=== QA v5 session 011 — TEST-INTEGRITY AUDIT (Audit C) ===
Date: 2026-09-26

--- C.1 Enumerate daemon-spawning tests ---
$ grep -rn "target/debug/tbard|CARGO_BIN_EXE|Command::new" src/ tests/

Daemon-spawning tests (3 total):
  1. src/lifecycle.rs:208  test_sigterm_releases_master
     Spawns via: std::env::current_exe().parent().parent().join("tbard")
     NOT env!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_tbard")
  2. tests/exit_code.rs:14 test_startup_failure_exits_nonzero
     Spawns via: std::env::current_exe().parent().parent().join("tbard")
     NOT env!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_tbard")
  3. src/providers/sim_display.rs tests (test_sim_display_acquires_vkms)
     Does NOT spawn the daemon — calls SimDisplayProvider::acquire() in-process.
     (Not a spawn-based test; listed for completeness.)

VERDICT C.1: ZERO tests use env!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_tbard"). Both spawn-based
  tests (lifecycle.rs, exit_code.rs) resolve the binary by relative path
  from current_exe() (deps → debug → tbard). ADR-028's claim "binary-
  spawning tests live in tests/ via env!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_tbard")" is
  REFUTED:
  - tests/exit_code.rs uses current_exe() path-resolution, NOT CARGO_BIN_EXE.
  - test_sigterm_releases_master lives in src/lifecycle.rs (a UNIT test),
    NOT in tests/.
  The CARGO_BIN_EXE migration is PARTIAL (effectively zero — no test uses
  the macro). W1 confirmed.

--- C.2 ci-gate builds --bin tbard before tests ---
$ cat scripts/ci-gate.sh
  [ADR 028 comment] build the main daemon binary BEFORE tests. cargo test
  does NOT rebuild target/debug/tbard; spawn-based tests need a fresh
  binary or they FAIL with a stale-binary REGRESSION.
  echo "==> cargo build --bin tbard"
  cargo build --bin tbard  [runs before clippy/check-invariants]

VERDICT C.2: ci-gate DOES build --bin tbard first. Within ci-gate, the
  stale-binary hazard is mitigated. But bare `cargo test` does NOT.

--- C.3 Adversarial: delete target/debug/tbard, run cargo test ---
$ rm -f target/debug/tbard
$ ls -la target/debug/tbard
ls: cannot access 'target/debug/tbard': No such file or file or directory
$ cargo test --test exit_code
running 1 test
test test_startup_failure_exits_nonzero ... ok
test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out
$ cargo test test_sigterm_releases_master
test lifecycle::tests::test_sigterm_releases_master ... ok
test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 40 filtered out

VERDICT C.3: STALE-BINARY FALSE-PASS CONFIRMED. After deleting
  target/debug/tbard, `cargo test` does NOT rebuild it. Both spawn-based
  tests SKIP (binary-not-found path → current_exe().parent().parent()
  .join("tbard").exists() returns false → eprintln skip → return → "ok"
  pass). The tests PASS against NOTHING. This is the EXACT QA v4 live
  regression (stale/absent binary → false pass), now reproducible at will
  outside ci-gate. ci-gate builds first, so the hazard is contained WITHIN
  ci-gate, but bare `cargo test` (the common dev invocation) is unsafe.
  ADR-028's claim "NO test spawns target/debug/tbard by path" is REFUTED:
  both spawn-based tests resolve by path (current_exe-derived), and both
  false-pass when the binary is absent.